/* ============================================================
   STUTI — Mahāgaṇapati Sahasranāma: the names, one at a time
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   Unlike the Viṣṇu and Lalitā registries, which were keyed from a
   nāmāvalī, this one is derived from the app's own mūla: the hymn's
   hundred and seventy name-ślokas already carry a gloss per name in
   Telugu, English and Hindi, so each name here is one word of that
   text with the three glosses that stood against it. Sandhi is undone
   for the citation form — gaṇeśvaro becomes Gaṇeśvaraḥ — and a name
   that is grammatically two words (bhūtānāṁ patiḥ) is kept whole.
   Editions divide the compounds differently and so count differently;
   this division yields 1059, and `note` says so in the glossary
   rather than rounding the number down to the traditional thousand.
   `slokaCounts` is how many names each of the 170 ślokas carries —
   the reader prints the range under the verse number.
   ============================================================ */
